    kv-cache: bound the payoff of removing the host KV store
    
    N5 -- writing new KV rows into pinned host memory directly from CUDA -- was
    the structural candidate this lane kept deferring to, and Experiment 026
    closed by naming it as the prerequisite for retrying overlap. Building it
    means two ggml buffers over one allocation plus a fork-local predicate at the
    scheduler's split-input sites, because placement consults supports_buft and
    supports_op jointly while copy elision consults supports_buft alone. Before
    paying for that, measure what it buys.
    
    GGML_KV_STORE_CEILING retargets the store at a scratch device tensor of the
    body's shape. The graph keeps its shape and its indices stay valid, but the
    store now runs entirely on CUDA: no device-to-host stage copy, no CPU
    set_rows, and the per-layer splits collapse. Attention still reads the host
    body host-to-device. Output is incorrect; this is an upper bound on N5 and
    nothing else, since a real N5 would additionally pay for a kernel writing
    across PCIe rather than into device memory.
    
    A/B/A/B, llama-bench -n 128:
    
      depth  4,096, r=5: store 31.7528/31.7305, removed 31.7514/31.7460  (+0.02%)
      depth 32,768, r=3: store 13.0294/13.0275, removed 13.0524/13.0518  (+0.18%)
    
    Removing the entire store side -- 32 blocking device-to-host copies, 32 CPU
    set_rows nodes, and 32 of the 33 scheduler splits per token -- is worth 0.18%
    at the depth where it is largest, and nothing at 4,096.
    
    This rejects N5, and N3 with it: splitting the per-token copy into a stable
    prefix and one new row exists to remove the write-then-read dependency the
    store creates, and removing that dependency completely does not make the token
    faster. It also falsifies this lane's recorded attribution that the store side
    is the serializer. The drains are free because the token is already bound on
    the host-to-device read of the body and the GPU has no independent work to do
    during the store windows.
    
    Reverted with the other measurement-only changes once dispositioned.
    
